<title>GREECE: DEVELOPMENT FUND TP PAY 96 DIV JUNE 17.</title>
<headline>DEVELOPMENT FUND TP PAY 96 DIV JUNE 17.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Closed-end Development Fund</p>
<p>will start paying its fiscal 1996 dividend on Tuesday</p>
<p>June 17.</p>
<p>Shareholders with coupon 22 will get a dividend per share of</p>
<p>70 drachmas.</p>
<p>Based on its net asset value (NAV) per share on June 9 --</p>
<p>1,150 drachmas -- the shares were trading at a discount of 17</p>
<p>percent. They closed at 940 drachmas on Friday, up 20.</p>
<p>The fund said its year-to-June 9 profits reached 450 million</p>
<p>drachmas and reported the following portfolio allocation:</p>
<p>    Domestic equities    79 percent</p>
<p>    Foreign equities	8</p>
<p>    Greek bonds	    11</p>
<p>    Foreign bonds	   1</p>
<p>    Cash			1</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
